%% SQS Message Flow Details
%% Shows pymysql-based consumer (auto-triggered)
%% Note: An ORM-based consumer exists but requires manual invocation

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Producer<br/>(FastAPI or Lambda)
    participant Q as SQS Queue
    participant L as Lambda Consumer<br/>(pymysql - auto-triggered)
    participant DB as MySQL
    participant DLQ as Dead Letter Queue

    Note over P,DLQ: Happy Path - Auto-triggered pymysql Consumer
    P->>Q: SendMessage<br/>{name, description, price, quantity}
    Note over Q: Message stored<br/>MessageId generated
    Q-->>P: MessageId: "abc-123"

    Q->>L: Event Source Mapping triggers<br/>ReceiveMessage (batch of 10)
    Note over L: Process each record<br/>using pymysql
    L->>DB: INSERT INTO items (...)
    DB-->>L: Success
    Note over Q: Message deleted<br/>automatically on success

    Note over P,DLQ: Failure Path
    Q->>L: ReceiveMessage
    L->>DB: INSERT INTO items (...)
    DB-->>L: Error (e.g., constraint violation)
    L-->>Q: Throw exception
    Note over Q: Message becomes<br/>visible after 60s

    loop Retry up to 3 times
        Q->>L: ReceiveMessage (same message)
        L->>DB: INSERT (retry)
        DB-->>L: Error
        L-->>Q: Throw exception
    end

    Note over Q: ReceiveCount > 3
    Q->>DLQ: Move message
    Note over DLQ: Manual investigation<br/>14 day retention

    Note over P,DLQ: Alternative: ORM Consumer (Manual Only)
    Note over L: sqs-consumer-orm Lambda uses<br/>SQLAlchemy ORM but is NOT<br/>auto-triggered by SQS
